    ("h2", "4.5 Inference Pipeline"),
    ("p", "The default mode (\"hybrid\") of MusicSeparationPipeline.separate follows Section 3.6. The recording is resampled to 44.1 kHz stereo. The 6-source model runs on the full song with an overlap of 0.25 and one random shift. The U-Net runs over 6 s chunks of the 22.05 kHz mono signal with 50% overlap, a Hann-weighted overlap-add and a 3x3 average filter over the resulting mask. Its masks are placed on the 44.1 kHz frame grid, which has the same frame rate and bin width, and the bins above 11 kHz reuse the top U-Net bin. Because the U-Net works at 22.05 kHz, frequencies above about 11 kHz are not modelled by it, and the extension of its highest mask value over that region is an engineering approximation that may limit high-frequency separation of violin, mridangam and ghatam. The competitive mask of Equation ({E:share}) is then applied and the loudness step runs. Table {T:infer} lists the constants."),
